userStories.description:
**Goal** — Define the shared finding policy, defaults and writer-authorized per-PR scope ruling.

**Motivation** — A scope ruling posted as a PR comment worked only as long as the reviewer re-read it.

**Approach** — `BotConfigSchema` (`config/schemas-bot.ts`) gains flat keys `blockingTriggers: z.array(z.enum(FINDING_TRIGGERS)).min(1).default(["normal", "own-concurrency"])` and `chainNoticeGeneration: z.number().int().min(1).default(2)`, each with a description in `cli/config-descriptions.ts`; the hand-written `BotConfig` interface (`config/runtime-types-bot.ts`) gains optional `blockingTriggers?: readonly FindingTrigger[]` and `chainNoticeGeneration?: number`. `NaxConfig.bot` is optional (`config/runtime-types.ts:383`), so every consumer reads the keys only through `configuredBlockingTriggers(config)` and `configuredChainNoticeGeneration(config)`, which return `DEFAULT_BLOCKING_TRIGGERS` and `DEFAULT_CHAIN_NOTICE_GENERATION` when `bot` or the key is absent. `blocking-findings/index.ts` gains `isBlockingFinding`, `readFindingThreadFacts`, `firstIssueLine`, `effectiveBlockingTriggers`, `configuredBlockingTriggers` and `configuredChainNoticeGeneration`.

`readFindingThreadFacts` reads the severity from the leading `**Critical**` / `**Important**` / `**Minor**` label (absent label = `important`, as `mergeEarlier` does today) and the trigger from a line starting `Trigger: <class>` (absent or unknown = `normal`). `firstIssueLine` drops a leading `**<Severity>** (<kind>): ` prefix, drops every line starting `Trigger:` or `Lineage:`, and returns the first remaining non-empty line, trimmed. A scope ruling is a top-level PR comment whose author is in `writers` and whose first non-empty line, trimmed and compared case-insensitively, matches `blocking triggers: <class>[, <class>...]`; a line starting `>`, `-` or `*` is not a match. Every class must be one of the four and the list must be non-empty, otherwise the comment is ignored and its first line is reported in `invalid`. The newest matching comment (by `createdAt`) wins. Any non-empty subset is allowed, narrower or wider than config.

Extend the nested barrel from US-001; use only `import type` for `PrComment`, `WorkflowSeverity` and config types. Have `mergeEarlier` use the shared reader while retaining the optional trigger on old threads. Update only the exact parsed-default objects at `test/unit/config/bot-config.test.ts:9`, `:10`, `:63` and `:64` for the additive keys. Agents receive facts, never orders: no prompt text tells them what to do with a trigger or a lineage.

**Scope** — In: pure helpers, config validation/defaults/descriptions, and interpretation of authorized scope comments. Out: US-003 posting/readiness wiring, US-008 status/notice wiring, and per-package `.nax/mono/<pkg>/config.json` values.

**Interface**
```typescript
export const DEFAULT_BLOCKING_TRIGGERS: readonly FindingTrigger[] = ["normal", "own-concurrency"];
/** Critical or important AND trigger in the set; an absent trigger reads "normal". */
export function isBlockingFinding(
  finding: { readonly severity: WorkflowSeverity; readonly trigger?: FindingTrigger },
  blocking: readonly FindingTrigger[],
): boolean;
/** Severity and trigger read back from a bot finding thread body (first comment). */
export function readFindingThreadFacts(body: string): { severity: WorkflowSeverity; trigger: FindingTrigger };
/** The plain first line of a finding issue: no severity label, no Trigger:/Lineage: lines. */
export function firstIssueLine(issue: string): string;
export const DEFAULT_CHAIN_NOTICE_GENERATION = 2;
/** `config.bot` is optional on NaxConfig: absent keys read as the defaults. */
export function configuredBlockingTriggers(config: { readonly bot?: { readonly blockingTriggers?: readonly FindingTrigger[] } }): readonly FindingTrigger[];
export function configuredChainNoticeGeneration(config: { readonly bot?: { readonly chainNoticeGeneration?: number } }): number;
/** The effective set for one PR: the newest writer scope-ruling comment, else the configured set. */
export function effectiveBlockingTriggers(input: {
  readonly comments: readonly PrComment[];
  readonly writers: ReadonlySet<string>;
  readonly configured: readonly FindingTrigger[];
}): { triggers: readonly FindingTrigger[]; source: "config" | { readonly commentId: string; readonly author: string }; invalid: readonly string[] };
```

**Goal** — Persist the bot's bounded history of successful fix pushes in its own fix-summary comment.

**Motivation** — #2982 and #2987 (points 1 and 3): no record links a finding to the bot fix that wrote its lines, so no signal says the findings are chasing their own fixes.

**Approach** — New `packages/nax/src/bot/push-ledger.ts`. The block is one line `<!-- nax-bot:pushes v1 <base64 of JSON array> -->`, which `markerPattern` does not match. `withPushLedger` replaces an existing block or inserts one immediately before the body's `nax-bot:v1` marker line; an empty list writes no block. `appendPushEntry` keeps the newest `MAX_PUSH_ENTRIES`, then drops the oldest entries until the encoded block is at most `MAX_LEDGER_CHARS` characters (a single entry over the budget keeps only its first items that fit). `readPushLedger` returns `unreadable: true` and no entries for a block whose base64 or JSON does not parse or whose entries lack `base`, `sha` (40 hex) or `items`. An item's `issue` is `firstIssueLine` of the agreed item's issue, capped at 120 characters. The finding arm of `AgreedItem` gains optional `lineage?: FindingLineage` and `lineageUnknown?: true` (US-005 sets them). `reportStep` (`bot/fix-report.ts`) reads the ledger from the own `fix-summary` comment in `env.own`, appends `{ base: env.info.headSha, sha: state.pushedSha, at: <ISO now>, items: <one per env.review.agreed item: key, item.lineage?.generation ?? 0, issue> }` when `state.outcome === "pushed"`, and writes the body through `withPushLedger`; every other outcome carries the read entries forward unchanged. An unreadable block is replaced by the new entries only and logged at warn. The ready-only summary rewrite `nameWaiverInSummary` (`bot/ci-waiver-ready.ts:149`) keeps the block as a non-readiness line.

**Line budget.** `bot/fix-report.ts` is at 596 of the 600-line source limit (`bun run check:file-sizes`, not grandfathered). US-004 first moves the private `outcomeText` function (about 45 lines) unchanged into new `bot/fix-outcome-text.ts`, which `renderFixSummary` imports; the ledger read-append-write lives in `push-ledger.ts` as `ledgerBody(previous: string | undefined, entry: BotPushEntry | undefined, body: string): string`. Every later story keeps `fix-report.ts` at or under 600 lines by putting new logic in the new modules named here.

A missing summary is an empty ledger; the first push posts it. Summary edit failure after a push surfaces as it does today; no entry is recorded. The ledger marker is separate from the identity marker. The ready-only path skips reportStep and must preserve retained entries. An advisor-ledger-only push retains outcome `nothing` and is not an `outcome: "pushed"` fix entry.

**Scope** — In: storage codec, retention, report writes, and ready-only preservation. Out: US-005 lineage calculation, US-007 follow-up text, US-008 convergence notices, and recording or retrying a failed summary write.

**Interface**
```typescript
export interface BotPushItem { readonly key: string; readonly generation: number; readonly issue: string }
export interface BotPushEntry { readonly base: string; readonly sha: string; readonly at: string; readonly items: readonly BotPushItem[] }
export interface FindingLineage { readonly generation: number; readonly parents: readonly string[]; readonly pushSha: string }
export const MAX_PUSH_ENTRIES = 64;
/** Encoded block budget, well under the forge's 65,536-character comment limit. */
export const MAX_LEDGER_CHARS = 24_000;
export function readPushLedger(body: string): { entries: readonly BotPushEntry[]; unreadable: boolean };
export function withPushLedger(body: string, entries: readonly BotPushEntry[]): string;
export function appendPushEntry(entries: readonly BotPushEntry[], entry: BotPushEntry): readonly BotPushEntry[];
function ledgerBody(previous: string | undefined, entry: BotPushEntry | undefined, body: string): string;
```
